ic hurricane season runs from June 1 to November 30, with peak activity occurring in August, September, and October. Major hurricanes, classified as Category 3 or higher on the [Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Wind Scale](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/aboutsshws.php), have sustained wind speeds of at least 111 miles per hour (178 km/h) and can cause significant damage and loss of life.\n\nAs of August 2026, no major hurricanes have taken place during the 2026 season, with only 4 named storms and a total [accumulated cyclone energy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accumulated_cyclone_energy) of only 3.2.\n\nOn August 6, [NOAA released](https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/outlooks/hurricane.shtml) a forecast of a 70% probability for the following ranges:\n\n* 7-13 Named Storms, including the 2 named storms that had been recorded to that point\n* 2-6 Hurricanes\n* 0-2 Major Hurricanes\n* Accumulated Cyclone Energy (ACE) range of 30-90% of the median, including the 3% that had been recorded to that point\n\nIf fewer than 2 Major Hurricanes occur, it would be the fewest since 2013.","resolution_criteria":"This question will resolve as the number of major Atlantic hurricanes that occur between June 1, 2026, and November 30, 2026, inclusive, as reported by the [National Hurricane Center (NHC)](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/?atlc) of the United States National Weather Service on December 1, 2026.","fine_print":"The question will be resolved using storm reports and data published by the National Hurricane Center as of December 1, 2026. Any subsequent revisions upgrading or downgrading a storm's intensity will not be considered. The NHC [Tropical Cyclone Advisory Archive](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/archive/2024/) and [Monthly Atlantic Tropical Weather Summary](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/text/MIATWSAT.shtml) may be used.","short_title":"How many Major Atlantic Hurricanes will occur in the 2026 Atlantic season?","post_id":45381,"aggregations":{"recency_weighted":{"history":null,"latest":null,"scor